module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.ClassGame

/-!
# The game with cyclic classes excludes `00000000011111001`, `00011011111111001` and `00000000010010001`

[ClassGame](ClassGame.md) proves, for any block with a valid `ClassCert`, that no column of the orbit of a row with a
leftmost 1 repeats it (`class_column`). The class-test survey at period 17 finds five blocks that the class test closes
at 16 cells and that nothing else in this repository or the kit excludes: four that the plain game does not close at 16
cells, and one that it closes at 15 cells and not at 14. This module proves the exclusion of `00000000011111001`,
`00011011111111001` and `00000000010010001`, each from a certificate at the least width at which the class test closes
it, made by `computations/class_blocks_wide.py`. The other blocks are in [ClassBlocks17Mid](ClassBlocks17Mid.md),
[ClassBlocks17Wide](ClassBlocks17Wide.md).

For each block `b` there is one section with the certificate `cls<b>`, one kernel check per width and phase and one per
phase of the classes, and the theorems `column_not_<b>` (every column of every row with a leftmost 1),
`center_not_<b>` (the center column) and `not_eventually_<b>` (the kit's form).

The natural-language argument is `ClassBlocks17.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata
open Rule30StripCertificateTable (wordOf)

